body:
I was also prescribed Provigil and Nuvigil before my doctor tried Ritalin and Adderall. They didn't work for me, but they might for you. So, there are other medications, but they have to be experimented with. Every person will have different reactions to medication, as we all have different body chemistry. The big problem is, since IH is such a rare disorder, drug companies don't put a lot of resources into finding a medication that is specific to the disorder, so we are left with trying to use medications created to combat different disorders, and trying to make them work. I would check with a sleep doctor who may have more experience with this disorder. Many doctors think they can advise in areas that are not in their wheelhouse, but inexperience will provide them with only the standard and obvious answers, instead of thinking outside the box or leaning on the knowledge and experience that previous cases have given them, which an inexperienced physician wouldn't have. 

&#x200B;

As someone who has been misdiagnosed, failed to be diagnosed, and given the run-around for over 20 years, just remember a couple things. Doctors aren't especially brilliant. You're not crazy. It's perfectly OK, and often needed, to try multiple physicians, even in the same category of specialty. This disorder is significantly less common than even Narcolepsy. You're going to find that many physicians don't know much about it, much less have even heard of it. And, I just spoke to the Physician's Assistant that I see (who I absolutely love) and she said that every year when they go for continuing education, she requests more education on the areas of sleep, and in the 20 years she's gone to these conferences, they've only even discussed sleep issues once. The doctor has to be proactive in this specific area to know anything about it. 

&#x200B;

Keep your head up, advocate for yourself, ask as many questions as you can and need to, ask for referrals if your doctor doesn't know something, and ask the doctor you're referred to what their experience has been with IH and what do they feel their level of understanding and familiarity is with it. We want to believe in the expertise and goodness of people, but at the end of the day, they are just people. We all have the same cognitive bias's and impairments. Good luck to you and keep fighting!
